  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Duvoglustat and Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase through a series of molecular interactions involving dehydrobruceine B. Duvoglustat is predicted to target multiple proteins, including Cell division cycle 2-like protein kinase 6, Cyclin-dependent kinase-like 3, and Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2, which are all targets of dehydrobruceine B. Dehydrobruceine B itself is identified as a target of Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase, indicating a potential pathway where Duvoglustat may modulate the activity of dehydrobruceine B, which in turn affects Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Duvoglustat influences Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase remains unclear. The evidence highlights a network of targets and interactions, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship between Duvoglustat and Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase."
